WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.988 --> 00:00:15.371
had always wanted to be on stage, but not like this.

2
00:00:16.172 --> 00:00:19.034
He was quickly sold to a circus to perform tricks.

3
00:00:19.975 --> 00:00:21.937
But the circus people were not kind.

4
00:00:23.498 --> 00:00:25.180
"Here you are, Donkey.

5
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.004
Have some straw for dinner," the trainer said, dumping it on the floor.

6
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.641
Pinocchio tasted a bite of straw.

7
00:00:33.181 --> 00:00:35.062
It was dry and tasted like dirt.

8
00:00:35.082 --> 00:00:39.205
"Hee-haw," he complained, and spit it out.

9
00:00:39.225 --> 00:00:42.046
"What, you don't like straw?

10
00:00:42.747 --> 00:00:46.529
Well, have some hay," the trainer said, dumping it on the floor.

11
00:00:47.209 --> 00:00:51.131
Pinocchio tasted a bite of hay, and it was as bad as the straw.

12
00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:56.294
"Hee-haw, hee-haw," Pinocchio complained.

13
00:00:56.314 --> 00:00:58.996
"Just you wait, little donkey.

14
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.283
You will be so hungry you will eat anything," said the trainer.

15
00:01:03.903 --> 00:01:05.564
And he whipped Pinocchio on the legs.

16
00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:09.807
Every day, the trainer would make Pinocchio practice.

17
00:01:09.827 --> 00:01:12.369
"Jump through this hoop.

18
00:01:12.929 --> 00:01:14.270
Walk on two legs.

19
00:01:14.691 --> 00:01:16.091
Dance the cha-cha.

20
00:01:16.852 --> 00:01:17.873
Balance a ball.

21
00:01:18.653 --> 00:01:21.715
Play dead," he would yell and snap his whip.

22
00:01:22.436 --> 00:01:25.198
If Pinocchio made a mistake, the trainer would whip him.

23
00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:31.643
One day, the trainer said, "Donkey, your first performance is tonight.

24
00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:34.685
If you do well, I will feed you grapes.

25
00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:39.209
If you make one mistake, I will feed you nothing."

26
00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:41.992
The circus tent filled with people.

27
00:01:42.592 --> 00:01:45.014
There were so many people that every seat was taken.

28
00:01:46.456 --> 00:01:51.720
"Ladies and Gentlemen, welcome to Vito's Circus," said the circus owner.

29
00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:55.724
"I am Vito, and we have a special show tonight.

30
00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.403
This donkey has traveled all the way from Spain to entertain you.

31
00:02:00.824 --> 00:02:02.985
He has danced for queens and kings.

32
00:02:03.406 --> 00:02:05.587
He has jumped for dukes and lords.

33
00:02:05.887 --> 00:02:08.910
He has amazed children all over Europe."

34
00:02:10.891 --> 00:02:14.094
The crowd cheered and clapped, and Pinocchio did his tricks.

35
00:02:14.774 --> 00:02:16.375
First, he walked on two legs.

36
00:02:16.976 --> 00:02:18.137
Then, he balanced a ball.

37
00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:22.020
The crowd was smiling, and Pinocchio could see the happy children.

38
00:02:24.864 --> 00:02:26.405
Then, he danced the cha-cha.

39
00:02:27.125 --> 00:02:30.967
Pinocchio looked at the crowd again, and he noticed a woman with blue hair.

40
00:02:31.887 --> 00:02:34.928
Pinocchio jumped through the hoop and then ran out of the tent.

41
00:02:35.848 --> 00:02:38.890
The crowd cheered, and Pinocchio ran and ran.

42
00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.532
Pinocchio didn't stop running until he got to the sea.

43
00:02:44.292 --> 00:02:46.593
There, by the water, stood the Blue Fairy!

44
00:02:46.613 --> 00:02:51.135
"Oh, Blue Fairy, was that you in the tent?"

45
00:02:51.795 --> 00:02:52.555
asked Pinocchio.

46
00:02:52.575 --> 00:02:55.464
"Yes, Pinocchio," she said.

47
00:02:55.484 --> 00:02:58.265
"Oh, I am so ashamed.

48
00:02:58.705 --> 00:03:01.446
I was foolish, and I was not a good boy.

49
00:03:01.466 --> 00:03:02.906
I am sorry.

50
00:03:03.506 --> 00:03:04.347
Can you help me?"

51
00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:07.547
"I know you are sorry, Pinocchio.

52
00:03:08.148 --> 00:03:10.228
But I cannot help you anymore.

53
00:03:11.148 --> 00:03:14.169
You must pay for your mistakes," she said sadly.

54
00:03:14.189 --> 00:03:18.170
"But, I don't want to be a donkey forever.

55
00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.191
I want to be a boy again.

56
00:03:20.711 --> 00:03:22.051
I want to go to school.

57
00:03:22.511 --> 00:03:25.192
And I want to save Geppetto," he cried.

58
00:03:25.212 --> 00:03:28.153
"Perhaps you will do all those things.

59
00:03:28.753 --> 00:03:31.574
But first, you must undo your mistakes.

60
00:03:32.474 --> 00:03:34.135
How did you become a donkey?"

61
00:03:34.655 --> 00:03:35.135
she asked.

62
00:03:35.155 --> 00:03:39.476
"I was selfish and lazy," Pinocchio answered.

63
00:03:39.496 --> 00:03:46.758
"Yes, and if you do the opposite, you will return to being a wooden boy," she said, then

64
00:03:46.798 --> 00:03:52.360
disappeared. "The opposite of selfish and lazy is generous and hardworking.

65
00:03:53.288 --> 00:03:55.853
How can I be generous and hardworking?"

66
00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:56.835
he wondered.

67
00:03:57.577 --> 00:03:59.000
Then, Pinocchio got an idea.
